  "reason": "Evidence: The current best configuration is config_030 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) with acc=0.632. All completed experiments have used resnet50 as the image encoder; the image encoder architecture is a completely unexplored, high-impact design dimension given that adding the image modality was the single largest gain observed (0.485→0.619). Question tested: Does upgrading the image encoder from ResNet50 to a stronger pretrained ViT-L (imagenet_vit_l) improve performance when all other settings are held at their best-known values (multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool, concat)? Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable extension of the current best, isolating the image encoder effect while keeping the already-validated choices (multiprofile > singleprofile, scvi_n200 ≥ pca_n2000, avgpool > transformer, concat ≈ weighted). A positive result would identify a new promising direction; a null result would confirm ResNet50 is sufficient and redirect budget toward other unexplored dimensions (e.g., scgpt encoder or fusion strategy). Under a limited budget, resolving this major architectural question is more informative than testing smaller variations (e.g., weighted vs. concat fusion, which showed negligible difference)."
}

